<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  com.wpnews.edition — file a front page twice a day, and serve it in between.

  Two editions, chosen against the New York session rather than against the clock:

    06:00 KST   the morning paper. The US close is 05:00 KST (06:00 in winter), so this is the
                first moment a complete day exists to report on.
    22:00 KST   the evening paper, half an hour before the US open, so the board shows what is
                about to happen rather than what already did.

  Twice, not more. A refresh on this panel takes twenty-five to thirty seconds and flashes the whole
  sheet; a board that does that six times a day is a board people stop looking at. The device also
  fingerprints every snapshot and skips the refresh entirely when nothing it draws has changed, so
  filing more often costs nothing but rarely buys anything either.

  Install:
      cp agent/standalone/com.wpnews.edition.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
      launchctl load  ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.wpnews.edition.plist
      launchctl start com.wpnews.edition            # file one now, to check it works

  The paths below are absolute because launchd does not run a login shell — it has no PATH worth
  the name, no nvm, no pyenv, and no idea where `claude` lives. Every one of those is a real way
  this fails silently at 6am, which is why PATH is spelled out rather than inherited.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.wpnews.edition</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/Users/ggrrm/Documents/wp_news_esp32/agent/standalone/file-edition.sh</string>
    </array>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin:/Users/ggrrm/.local/bin</string>
        <key>HOME</key>
        <string>/Users/ggrrm</string>
        <key>EDITION_DIR</key>
        <string>/Users/ggrrm/.wpnews/edition</string>
    </dict>

    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <array>
        <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>6</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>0</integer></dict>
        <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>22</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>0</integer></dict>
    </array>

    <!-- launchd already fires a missed StartCalendarInterval as soon as the machine wakes, which is
         what saves a board that would otherwise show yesterday's paper because a lid was shut.
         RunAtLoad is separate and off: loading the agent should not spend an API call. -->
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/ggrrm/.wpnews/edition/log/launchd.out</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/ggrrm/.wpnews/edition/log/launchd.err</string>
</dict>
</plist>
